From 863aaeb03055b8942ae7aeeb5e983ffe2c4bc08e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emanuele Bottelli <bottelliemanuele@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:49:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i18n: the macOS application menu follows the interface
 language

AppKit builds the application menu (About, Services, Hide, Hide Others,
Show All, Quit) in English for apps without a nib, and winit's default
menu is one, so it stayed English while the rest of PdfCraft was in the
user's language.

- vendor/winit, patch (12): `platform::macos::set_app_menu_titles`, a
  safe function that retitles the standard items, finding each by its
  action and the Services item by its submenu; a main menu the app
  replaced is left alone.
- ui-egui: `PdfCraftApp::on_language`, told the interface language once
  at start and on every change of the preference (Preferences, `ui.set`,
  restore), and asked again next frame while it says it is not done.
- apps/pdfcraft: `mac_menu` words the six titles from the catalog with
  `{app}` as the process name and applies them; English catalogs keep
  what AppKit showed.
- Italian and Lithuanian entries (the Lithuanian catalog must cover every
  bundled key); other catalogs fall back to English until translated.
- tests: `mac_menu` titles per language, `language_hook`, the vendored
  patch guard `winit_macos_app_menu`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
